{
  "_comment": "⛔ QUARANTINED scene styles (five-line split, Aaron 2026-08-12): this dormant bench's style blocks, vendored OUT of ui_theme.json (a scene's values belong in its scene file). They move into this bench's own .scene.json at its migration — do not grow this file. Colors are $token refs into ui_theme.json's theme.tokens; a `theme` key here is refused as a palette fork.",
  "paperdoll": {
    "_comment": "flicker-paperdoll's in-scene HUD (behaviour: Alpha/content/scripts/hud_paperdoll.lua). Replaces the POC keypress toggles + draw_text overlay. `inventory` = the equip-slot bar; a slot's piece is drawn only while its cell is lit. Slot keys are the contract with the engine: it publishes `slot_<key>_loaded`/`slot_<key>_on` on the Model and reads `slot_<key>` back. Sheaths have no cell by design — they are always worn (no sheath/unsheath animations yet).",
    "inventory": {
      "header": "$pd_inventory",
      "header_size": 13,
      "header_color": "$bronze",
      "slot": 54,
      "gap": 6,
      "pad": 12,
      "margin_b": 18,
      "panel_bg": "$panel_bg",
      "panel_border": "$sap_border",
      "label_size": 12,
      "cell": {
        "cell": "$stone3",
        "hot": "$sig_green",
        "label": "$ink",
        "label_size": 12
      },
      "empty": {
        "cell": "$stone1",
        "hot": "$stone1",
        "label": "$faint",
        "label_size": 12
      },
      "slots": [
        {
          "key": "hair",
          "label": "$pd_hair"
        },
        {
          "key": "neck",
          "label": "$pd_neck"
        },
        {
          "key": "chest",
          "label": "$pd_chest"
        },
        {
          "key": "legs",
          "label": "$pd_legs"
        },
        {
          "key": "glove_l",
          "label": "$pd_glove_l"
        },
        {
          "key": "glove_r",
          "label": "$pd_glove_r"
        },
        {
          "key": "boot_l",
          "label": "$pd_boot_l"
        },
        {
          "key": "boot_r",
          "label": "$pd_boot_r"
        },
        {
          "key": "rhand",
          "label": "$pd_r_hand"
        },
        {
          "key": "lhand",
          "label": "$pd_l_hand"
        }
      ]
    },
    "view": {
      "margin": 16,
      "top": 92,
      "row_h": 20,
      "box": 14,
      "label_x": 22,
      "label_size": 13,
      "label_color": "$ink",
      "checkbox": {
        "box": "$stone2",
        "check": "$rune_glow_hi",
        "border": "$edge4",
        "pad": 3
      },
      "attack": {
        "w": 120,
        "h": 24,
        "gap_y": 10,
        "label": "$pd_attack",
        "style": {
          "cell": "$hp_lo",
          "hot": "$hp_hi",
          "label": "$ink_bright",
          "label_size": 13,
          "hi": "$sheen",
          "shadow": "$stone0",
          "border": "$sig_red"
        }
      },
      "_items_note": "`animate` = the Animation/Pose toggle: on drives the pose from the pack's state machine (real runtime animation, blended), off is A-pose/bind (the fitting reference — Idle is an authored stance, already off bind). ↑/↓ cycle animation states, Space pauses. `blend` A/Bs the transition crossfade.",
      "items": [
        {
          "key": "animate",
          "label": "$pd_animate"
        },
        {
          "key": "blend",
          "label": "$pd_blend_xfade"
        },
        {
          "key": "show_mesh",
          "label": "$pd_mesh"
        },
        {
          "key": "show_textures",
          "label": "$pd_textures"
        },
        {
          "key": "show_skeleton",
          "label": "$pd_skeleton"
        },
        {
          "key": "show_collision",
          "label": "$pd_collision"
        }
      ]
    },
    "fit": {
      "_comment": "The fit gadget — shown only while a piece is selected (Model.fit_active). Click a piece in the scene to select it; click empty space to deselect. `offset` sliders are in WORLD axes at rest (x lateral, y depth, z up), NOT bone axes — the torso bones are tilted 90°, so bone-space nudging would be unusable by eye. Record writes every loaded piece's fit to musefit/fits.json.",
      "margin": 16,
      "w": 250,
      "pad": 12,
      "row_h": 26,
      "slider_h": 12,
      "label_w": 54,
      "value_w": 62,
      "header": "$pd_fit_prefix",
      "header_size": 14,
      "header_color": "$bronze",
      "panel_bg": "$panel_bg",
      "panel_border": "$bronze_dim",
      "label_size": 13,
      "label_color": "$ink",
      "value_size": 12,
      "value_color": "$dim",
      "slider": {
        "track": "$stone1",
        "fill": "$sap_base",
        "fill_hi": "$sap_border",
        "handle": "$sap_border",
        "handle_w": 9,
        "focus_track": "$stone3",
        "focus_fill": "$rune_glow",
        "focus_label": "$rune_glow_hi",
        "value_color": "$dim",
        "value_size": 12,
        "label_size": 13
      },
      "_focus_note": "Click a slider to FOCUS it; ←/→ then nudge it by `nudge` (hold Shift for `nudge_coarse`). A trackpad drag over a ~120px track spans the whole range, which is far too coarse to fit a piece by eye — the arrows are the fine control. The focused row is drawn with `focus_*`. SCALE IS PER-AXIS (sx/sy/sz): a garment generated separately from the body is rarely the same build, so a uniform scale can line it up but never make it fit. Scale and offset are both in WORLD axes at rest (x lateral, y depth, z up), NOT bone axes — the fit cancels the socket rest rotation, so x thickens sideways whichever bone the piece hangs off.",
      "focus_track": "$stone3",
      "focus_fill": "$rune_glow",
      "focus_label": "$rune_glow_hi",
      "uniform": {
        "min": 0.1,
        "max": 200.0,
        "nudge": 0.1,
        "nudge_coarse": 1.0
      },
      "scale": {
        "min": 0.25,
        "max": 4.0,
        "nudge": 0.01,
        "nudge_coarse": 0.1
      },
      "offset": {
        "min": -120.0,
        "max": 120.0,
        "nudge": 0.1,
        "nudge_coarse": 1.0
      },
      "rotate": {
        "min": -180.0,
        "max": 180.0,
        "nudge": 1.0,
        "nudge_coarse": 15.0
      },
      "_rows_note": "The gadget's rows, in panel order. SHARED CONTRACT: hud.lua lays them out and the engine cycles focus (↑/↓) and nudges (←/→) from this same list, so the order and keys cannot drift apart. `group` selects the row's min/max/nudge block above.",
      "rows": [
        {
          "key": "fit_u",
          "label": "$pd_size",
          "group": "uniform"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_sx",
          "label": "$pd_wide",
          "group": "scale"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_sy",
          "label": "$pd_thick",
          "group": "scale"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_sz",
          "label": "$pd_tall",
          "group": "scale"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_rx",
          "label": "$pd_pitch",
          "group": "rotate"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_ry",
          "label": "$pd_yaw",
          "group": "rotate"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_rz",
          "label": "$pd_roll",
          "group": "rotate"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_x",
          "label": "$pd_x_lat",
          "group": "offset"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_y",
          "label": "$pd_y_depth",
          "group": "offset"
        },
        {
          "key": "fit_z",
          "label": "$pd_z_up",
          "group": "offset"
        }
      ],
      "record": {
        "h": 26,
        "label": "$pd_record_all_to_content"
      },
      "status": {
        "size": 12,
        "gap_y": 5,
        "ok": "$sig_green",
        "err": "$hp_hi"
      },
      "button": {
        "cell": "$sap_base",
        "hot": "$sap_hover",
        "label": "$ink_bright",
        "label_size": 13,
        "glow": "$sap_glow",
        "hi": "$sheen",
        "border": "$sap_border"
      }
    },
    "stats": {
      "margin": 16,
      "top": 62,
      "size": 13,
      "color": "$ink"
    }
  },
